WEBVTT

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.340
Damn it...

00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:01.160
The 28th American President, 
Thomas Woodrow Wilson,

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.110
once said, "There are 
no coincidences in fate.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.780
Before humans encounter a particular fate,

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.390
they make it for themselves."

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:14.910
In other words, 
you lost because I was too strong.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.930
Was it carved into your soul?

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.550
Great work!

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.810
Nice job, Kodama-chan.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.940
Here, have a moist towel. Good work.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:28.970
Hibiki-san.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:30.200
Disinfectant.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.940
Sure, Kodama-chan!

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:35.690
An idol's handshakes are only for her fans!

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.650
The way you always
 remember the little things...

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.720
That's just what I expect from you, Kodama-chan.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.380
It was carved into my soul.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.200
There's no point carving it into my manager.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:48.810
Also, Kodama-chan, I hate to say 
this when you're busy, but...

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.210
We've already got our next gig lined up.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.220
I'm leaving the scheduling to you, Hibiki-san.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.050
Napoleon Bonaparte, 
the Emperor of France, once said,

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:06.980
"Happiness is having a job that 
matches your wishes and abilities."

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.660
In other words, keep getting me work.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.000
That's just what I wanted 
to hear, Kodama-chan!

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.480
So deep!

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.990
I wish your fans could have heard that!

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.350
Yeah.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.930
Maybe we should invite 
our eighth opponents

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:27.500
to a special concert where they can 
have Awaza Kodama all to themselves.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.000
That's our next offer.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.250
So you managed to make it 
through the first song.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:15.580
You know the difference in our strengths 
and keep fighting instead of giving up.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:19.440
I love it when people do that,
 Takatsuki Tazuna-kun.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.780
Akutagawa Koyori-chan.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:24.030
This attack wasn't a coincidence after all.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.990
But the English poet Geoffrey 
Chaucer once said,

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.540
"He who knows himself is a sage."

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:36.380
In other words, if you try to 
be a sage, you can't beat me.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.890
I think you need the courage 
to admit that, too.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.680
Hide once I give the signal.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.680
I'll look for a chance to charge.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.600
The concert's back on.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.150
<i>English poet John Dryden once said,</i>

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.900
<i>"Be slow in deciding, but fast in execution!"</i>

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.900
<i>That quick decision was amazing!</i>

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:08.250
She's not like the other Hand Shakers.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:12.910
The song I'm about to sing is just for you.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.760
Awaza Kodama, singing for just two people.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.170
It's a very valuable opportunity.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.800
Awaza Kodama... I've heard 
that name somewhere.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.540
Wait... She just gave me her true name!

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:28.300
Wait, you don't know Kodama-chan?

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:32.810
When did he get up there?

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.930
Wait, Kodama-chan!

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:39.710
These two don't know how 
impossible what they're seeing is.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:40.960
Poor things!

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.810
Poor, ignorant things!

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:43.820
<i>He's taking pity on us.</i>

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.320
Hibiki-san, that's a bad habit of yours.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:51.850
French philosopher Blaise Pascal once said,

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:55.830
"Do not fear ignorance. 
Fear false knowledge."

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:59.130
It's not a sin for them to be ignorant,

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:01.840
because that ignorance means innocence.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:05.770
They have pure souls as white as lilies,

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:08.600
and I'm about to carve the name

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.400
Awaza Kodama into them.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.620
And carve it deep!

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.140
A super idol!

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.310
How wonderful, Kodama-chan!

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:16.890
It was carved into me!

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:17.740
Excuse me.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.270
Good work!

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:21.800
I'm terribly sorry about earlier.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:25.720
I am Moriyama Hibiki from Echo Productions.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:26.780
Hibiki-san!

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.020
I wasn't on the job!

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.420
That was just reflex. I'm really sorry.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:32.890
Really sorry!

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:33.420
No...

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:35.790
Sorry for bothering you.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:39.000
If you want a handshake, sure.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.290
An idol's singing voice exists for her fans,

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:43.800
and so does her palm.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:47.420
I disinfect with alcohol after
 touching my manager's hand,

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.550
so he doesn't count.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:51.480
Now, let's get back to it!

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:53.610
Let it resound within you!

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.780
Carve it into your soul!

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.790
Sonic Sword!

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:12.840
<i>It doesn't mesh...</i>

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:14.780
<i>How did things end up like this...</i>

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.870
<i>How did this happen, again?</i>

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.370
Go shopping with these.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:22.370
The two of you.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.540
Have fun.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:27.800
Actually, you know,

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.300
I don't know what to buy for girl's clothes.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.300
Neither do I...

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:41.180
It's getting late, we need 
to decide what we're buying.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:46.360
Sorry, Koyori, I made you waste 
time walking to a bunch of places.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.530
Makihara-sensei shouldn't have 
just put me in charge of this.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.360
I don't know how this works!

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.160
You want me to choose?

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:57.930
Oh, I know.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.240
I can ask President Lily!

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.620
You swapped contact info a while ago.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.540
You want me to choose?

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:13.930
I guess I'll do my best.

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:17.800
<i>That's right. I went shopping with a girl...</i>

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:20.180
<i>with Koyori... for the first time.</i>

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:24.010
<i>It was the first time I'd eaten ice 
cream on the street with a girl.</i>

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.690
<i>It was the first time I'd 
chosen a girl's clothes.</i>

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.090
<i>I never thought</i>

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.450
<i>that would be a part of my life.</i>

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.320
<i>It was fun.</i>

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.910
<i>If I could go somewhere else with Koyori...</i>

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:41.830
<i>This time, I won't let go.</i>

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:55.220
Takatsuki Tazuna-kun and 
Akutagawa Koyori-chan, right?

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:58.790
She knows us?

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.760
<i>I was having fun, but...</i>

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:11.210
What is this power?

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.470
There are no openings in it!

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:13.940
Which means...

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.810
I can't see the other one.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.700
But at this rate, I can push through!

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.700
I'll have to do it!

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:29.000
Russian author Maxim Gorky once said,

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:34.010
"Talent is believing in yourself,
 and your own power!"

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:37.050
Single Gear is being pushed back so easily!

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.860
I believe in my power more than anybody.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:49.730
The power of Awaza Kodama!

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:53.050
What is this strength?

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:56.060
The power of her Nimrod is too different!

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.250
She let us go.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.080
Okay, Kodama-chan!

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.410
Okay! That's an okay!

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:11.080
A trap?

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.770
Excuse me, excuse me.

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:14.630
This is the end!

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:16.870
Hold still a moment.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:23.970
Okay, thank you for forming a line.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:27.660
The concert's not over yet.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.980
You're in such a hurry.

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:33.960
Time can be gold or lead, 
depending on how you use it.

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:38.240
Those are the words of Antoine Prévost.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:42.740
The concerts of Awaza Kodama 
are definitely gold, right?

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.990
Koyori, hang on tight!

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:55.930
This is a true combo attack!

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:03.900
Hibiki-san amplifies my shock waves!

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:14.460
The 28th American President, 
Thomas Woodrow Wilson,

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.070
once said, "There are 
no coincidences in fate.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.900
Before humans encounter a particular fate,

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:22.280
they make it for themselves."

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:26.690
Now, what is the fate that 
you've made for yourself?

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:29.420
To fight? To run?

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.960
I'll be waiting for the encore.

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.040
If you don't block this 
with everything you've got,

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:50.480
you really will die.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:14.200
Good work, Kodama-chan.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.740
Another easy victory.

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:17.590
It was carved into my soul.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:20.580
Kodama-chan?

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:24.970
In the end, they got us.

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:29.450
Looks like they want to see my concert again.

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.850
For an idol, that's a great honor.

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:42.620
<i>Koyori-kun!</i>

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:44.360
<i>Koyori-kun, what's wrong?</i>

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:45.870
<i>What happened?</i>

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:46.980
<i>Where's Tazuna-kun?</i>

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.370
<b>Makihara-sensei</b>

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.370
<b>Help</b>

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:06.230
I should've lost there...

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:11.220
I just got lucky.

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:34.040
Water-Free Ethanol

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:34.040
So you managed to escape the battle zone?

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:36.140
Smart move.

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:39.690
Their strength was literally insane.

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:41.800
It meshed...

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:46.700
And it was like their Nimrod 
was infecting the Ziggurat...

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:49.800
Until now, the place we've 
been in has changed, but....

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:54.470
The Nimrods have various 
effects on the Ziggurat.

00:13:55.780 --> 00:14:00.080
But, if their Nimrod is infecting 
the Ziggurat itself,

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:03.900
it's probably a Hand Shaker 
who's getting closer to God.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:08.670
The Hand Shakers gain the 
powers of those they defeat.

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:10.620
If you take out several opponents,

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:13.660
your Nimrod starts to infect the Ziggurat.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.760
I saw it a long time ago, just once.

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:19.670
Really, you did well to even escape.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:25.170
I wasn't strong enough...

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:30.970
I have to think... and think... and win.

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:34.680
If I don't win, Koyori will...

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:39.110
They're tough opponents, 
though, those Hand Shakers.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:42.310
You can't beat them right now.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:44.570
But I have to fight anyway!

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:51.260
It's obvious they were 
coming after you directly.

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:54.040
They should know that you escaped, too.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:57.330
Next time I won't be able to run.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:58.890
Don't worry.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:00.330
I'll be fine.

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:13.870
I've never let one escape before...

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:17.030
I fought yesterday and I've got 
a concert today. It's rough!

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:19.020
That's what makes it worth doing, though.

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:21.930
Well, it's always best to be busy.

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.900
I'm back.

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:25.900
Oh, Kodama-chan,

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:28.060
I got the water you asked for.

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:28.900
Thanks.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:32.250
I also got pudding you didn't ask for!

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:33.450
Thanks for that, too!

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:35.450
Are you tired?

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:38.600
Being both an idol and a Hand Shaker.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:40.960
Should I adjust our schedule?

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:43.690
It's nothing!

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:47.960
American theologist Edward Young said,

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:51.950
"Wasting time means having 
time stolen from you."

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:53.850
An idol who's so busy it could kill her

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:56.620
doesn't have time to waste 
with time thieves, right?

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:58.850
That's my Kodama-chan!

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:03.600
Then my job is to make your 
scheduling work, isn't it?

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:06.330
Don't you push yourself too hard either.

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:08.610
Kodama-chan, you're so nice!

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:13.100
Such a great song is being 
carved into my soul!

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:13.610
No, answer it.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.400
Yes, hello.

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.060
This is Moriyama with Echo Productions.

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:18.620
Yes.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.570
Yes. Yes.

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:22.560
No, not at all!

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.890
Is there anything you can do?

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:25.720
Yes...

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.500
All right.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:30.200
Thank you so much.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.340
What's wrong?

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.600
A problem, right?

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.220
N-Not at all!

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:37.570
Nothing at a—

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:38.390
Yes...

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:40.120
Tell me.

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:43.900
It's about our next concert.

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.900
They want to cancel it.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:50.580
President Nabeta got involved again.

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:51.830
I'm sorry.

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:54.400
Yeah, thanks.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:58.040
But it's not your fault.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:00.880
It's his fault for being angry 
at us when he's in the wrong.

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:03.910
He was the one who was inconsiderate.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:07.040
But I'm not worried at all.

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:09.720
Oh, Teshirogi-kun again?

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:12.950
He's really working hard, huh?

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:16.360
These hands are for my fans.

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:18.380
My voice is for my fans,

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:20.460
and my smiles are for my fans.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:23.150
It's all for all of my fans.

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:24.270
And, because of that,

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:27.310
I don't have time to get sad over 
interference from my pathetic president.

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:32.720
But is my talented manager 
getting sad over it?

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:34.590
You're right...

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:35.520
You're right!

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:37.070
That's my Kodama-chan!

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:40.020
I'm so moved I could cry!

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:43.080
It's carved into my soul!

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.330
Don't cry.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:50.840
I'm busy with my Hand Shaker job, too...

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:53.770
Next concert, I need to carve it

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:57.340
into the souls of Takatsuki 
Tazuna-kun and Akutagawa Koyori-chan!

00:17:57.990 --> 00:18:00.900
I need to carve my songs into their souls.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:04.120
Okay, get me that schedule!

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:05.480
Right, Kodama-chan.

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:09.110
They say "idol" used to be a religious term.

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:12.010
If idols are made in the image of God,

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:15.400
it's natural for an idol to become a god.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.490
It's inevitable.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.350
I'm going to win.

00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:20.990
As an idol, and a Hand Shaker.

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.450
Let's aim for God!

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:24.120
Yup!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.610
For the sake of our fans, too!

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:27.510
Right, Kodama-chan!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.020
Huh?

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.110
It's from Koyori-chan.

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:56.090
She wants to talk to me?

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:57.130
What is it?

00:18:57.590 --> 00:18:59.110
Of course, that's fine.

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:03.370
<b>This is Koyori. 
Sorry to contact you so late.

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:03.370
Tazuna-kun was hurt in a Hand Shaker fight?

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:08.460
If I knew about Koyori-chan's body,

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:10.870
would I not have fought?

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:13.200
I see.

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:15.770
She's upset that she doesn't 
have a Nimrod, huh?

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:17.960
That's right.

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:21.180
If I was Koyori-chan...

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:27.390
I didn't like how Masaru was 
hurt for my sake in the battle.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:31.640
I couldn't stand having 
my beloved brother hurt.

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:34.400
I didn't want him to just keep protecting me.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:38.140
But my Nimrod was weak...

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:40.230
All I could do was help Masaru.

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.280
I lost to the two of them,

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.490
but I learned what I could do for Masaru,

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:49.570
and what Masaru was doing for me.

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:51.160
We were able to understand each other.

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:56.920
That's why I'm sure there's something 
you can do for Tazuna-kun, too.

00:19:57.350 --> 00:19:59.590
He needs to notice himself.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:02.230
He needs to believe in you more.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:04.980
Masaru and I were able to do it.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:06.590
Sis?

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.590
You were saying all that out loud...

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:12.940
It was embarrassing to hear.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:15.390
I-It's not like that!

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:17.320
That was, um...

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:22.570
And why are you spending 
so much time in my room?

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:24.820
Because...

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:26.950
I wanted to be with you.

00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:14.360
<i>You were with me when I woke up.</i>

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:17.200
<i>You protected me when I knew nothing,</i>

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:18.810
<i>and you guided me.</i>

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:21.550
<i>You don't have to suffer alone anymore.</i>

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:23.080
<i>You don't need to feel pain.</i>

00:23:23.560 --> 00:23:25.380
<i>If you can't fight,</i>

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:26.710
<i>I will...</i>

00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:28.540
<i>And we will, together!</i>

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:33.910
<i>Next time on Hand Shakers, 
Episode 9: Finally Fairy.</i>

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:35.930
<i>I want you to accept me for who I am.</i>

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:39.160
<i>Forever. And everywhere.</i>
